Done — the board is implemented, tested, and the app is running with it.

## How the task list worked before

The main process owns SQLite and answers `tasks:list` by calling `listTasks()` in [main/tasks.ts](src/main/tasks.ts), which returns every task already ordered. [Tasks.tsx](src/renderer/src/modules/Tasks.tsx) kept that list in one `tasks` state, re-fetched it after every create/update/status/delete, and derived the visible rows with `filterTasks(tasks, { view, text, priority, project, tag }, today)` from [shared/tasks.ts](src/shared/tasks.ts) — the filter state itself lived inside the list component. That filtering is pure: view (Today/Upcoming/Overdue/All/Completed), text, priority, project and tag combined.

## What I added

**Shared filter hook.** The filter state and the `filterTasks` result now live in [useTaskFilters.ts](src/renderer/src/lib/useTaskFilters.ts). The Tasks page owns one instance; the list renders `filtered` and the board renders columns grouped from the *same* filter object. Filtering in either view changes the single shared state, so switching views preserves the filters exactly.

**Board view** ([TaskBoard.tsx](src/renderer/src/modules/TaskBoard.tsx)) — To do / In progress / Done columns built by `groupTasksForBoard()` in [shared/tasks.ts](src/shared/tasks.ts), which calls the same `filterTasks` the list uses. Cards show title, priority, due date with overdue highlighting, and checklist progress. Drag a card to another column to change status (existing `tasks:setStatus` IPC); drag within a column to reorder, saved through the existing `tasks:reorder` IPC via `applyColumnOrder()`, which keeps other columns' positions intact. No new dependency — HTML5 drag and drop. Clicking a card opens the same `TaskEditor` and the page refreshes after saving.

**View toggle + persistence.** A List / Board `seg` control lives beside the filter tabs. The choice is stored in the app's settings as `taskLayout` (added to `Settings`, `DEFAULT_SETTINGS` and `normalizeSettings`), so it survives restarts and invalid values fall back to `list`. The command palette now has **“Switch to Board view”** in [actions.ts](src/renderer/src/actions.ts), which navigates to Tasks and raises a `tasks:board` event.

**Accessibility.** Cards are real buttons with visible focus (the app's global `:focus-visible` outline), `Alt+←/→` moves a focused card between columns, Enter opens it, and column drop targets get an accent border/ring. Everything uses existing `card`, `badge`, `text-neg`, `bg-accent`, `bg-line` theme utilities — no hardcoded colors.

## How the views stay in sync

Both read one `tasks` array loaded through the same `window.api.tasks.list()` call and one `filter` object from `useTaskFilters`. Every mutation — the list's checkbox, bulk toolbar, editor save, or a board drop — calls the same IPC and then `refresh()`, which replaces that single array. There is no second store and no copied task state.

## Verification

- `npx tsc --noEmit` — clean.
- `npx tsx tests/tasks.ts` — **14/14 checks pass**, including new tests asserting the board's columns contain exactly the list's tasks for eight different filters (view, project, priority, tag, text, completed), the column-reorder slot mapping, and layout setting normalization.
- `npm run dev` — rebuilt and running with no errors in the log.

That test pass again required temporarily building `better-sqlite3` for Node, then rebuilding it for Electron so `npm run dev` works; that's the pre-existing single-binary limitation I noted earlier, not something this change introduced.
